      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks there\u0027s a bit of confusion here. There are two security concerns here:\n1. Mapping a page which is not owned by the host. This is what Dymtro is referring to I believe and should be addressed by something like:\n```\n\tunsigned long map_phys;\n\tpkvm_host_ept_lookup(pteval \u0026 VTD_PAGE_MASK, \u0026map_phys, NULL, NULL);\n\tif (map_phys \u003d\u003d INVALID_ADDR) {\n\t\tpkvm_err(\"pkvm: phys addr 0x%lx not mapped in host ept\\n\", pteval \u0026 VTD_PAGE_MASK);\n\t\treturn err;\n\t}\n```\nIn the shadow implementation, its taken care by [this](https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android16-6.12-desktop/arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/iommu.c#392)\n2. Donation of a page from host to hypervisor which is already DMA mapped by the host (solved by aosp/3586350), which has to be taken care separately.",
